Within the panel, the affected variants are rs16910526, rs1800896, rs2069705 and rs5743810 (10 study by
variant cells). All are handled by complementing the alleles.

rs7309123 is a C/G palindrome, so its strand cannot be settled from the allele letters. It was resolved study by study from
control allele frequencies, primer sequences and full texts (addenda 16, 19 and 21).


::: {#tbl-strand .cell tbl-cap='Strand of rs7309123 by study (A: resolved, high confidence; B: low to medium; C: weak or by inference; D: undetermined). From data/rs7309123_strand_resolution.csv.'}

```{.r .cell-code}
read.csv("data/rs7309123_strand_resolution.csv") |>
  transmute(Study = paste(first_author, year), Ancestry = ancestry, Strand = gsub("_", " ", strand_conclusion),
            Grade = grade, `In primary analysis` = ifelse(use_in_primary, "yes", "no")) |>
  arrange(Grade, Study) |>
  gt()
```

